-- Global exercise catalogue (WP92, decision 72, ADR-0047). Repeatable: Flyway re-runs this file when its checksum changes,
-- before R__plan_templates.sql (repeatables run in description order).
-- One exercise per distinct item of the seeded templates (same English texts, durations and es / id translations) plus
-- the Cooper test. Idempotent upserts keyed by stable UUIDs (uuid5 of the name key). Rows are only ever upserted, never
-- deleted: plan items of every academy may reference them. Written in English (locale 'en', the title / description
-- columns) with Spanish and Indonesian in i18n, as the templates are (ADR-0039); the service shows them in the caller's
-- language. The academies' own exercises (owner_tenant_id set) are never touched here.
--
-- Template items show the texts of their exercise: R__plan_templates.sql copies them when it runs, and the update at the
-- end of this file keeps them in step when only the catalogue changes. FORCE is lifted for the duration of this
-- transaction, as in R__plan_templates.sql, because global rows can only be written with the table owner exempted.
alter table athlete.exercise no force row level security;
alter table athlete.plan_item no force row level security;

